0,Music of Algeria - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Algeria,"For several centuries, Algerian music was dominated by styles inherited from Al-Andalus, eventually forming a unique North African twist on these poetic forms. Algerian music came to include suites called nuubaat (singular nuuba). Later derivatives include rabaab and hawzii.","Arabic, Algerian",Afro-Asiatic
1,Raï - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raï,"The music performed was called raï. It drew its name from the Algerian Arabic word raï ('opinion' or 'advice'), which was typically inserted—and repeated—by singers to fill time as they formulated a new phrase of improvised lyrics.","Arabic, Algerian",Afro-Asiatic
2,Algeria - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algeria,"Algeria, officially the People's Democratic Republic of Algeria, is a country in the Maghreb region of North Africa.Most Algerians identify as Arabs, while Berbers form a sizeable minority. Sunni Islam is the official religion and practised by 99 percent of the population.[12].","Arabic, Algerian",Afro-Asiatic
